Z||000000||VISCERAL||08-12-99||11:28 PM||||Hey there, for you guys who have the mustang hood scoop on your rear decklid, did you:<p>* Cut the center post in the opening          side-    probably<br>* Cut off the backing face in the opening-      of course<br>* What did you use for screening-<br>   hopefully metal<br>* Where did you get the screening? <br>* How did you mount the screening?--adhesive?
Z||000001||VISCERAL||08-12-99||11:40 PM||||Maybe I shouldn't use screening. Maybe when I cut the decklid I should put some trim edge guard on the edges to try to stop the water from dripping in. What do you guys use or don't you have a water dripping problem?<br>How much did it cost you to have it painted?<br>Did you just bolt it onto the hood bare or did you cement some felt or some type of rubber strip under the edges?
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||08-12-99||11:46 PM||||Did you see the post in the chat "REAR deck scoop". It looks like a easy bolt-on application, and the price is right.<p>I have one on order. I did think about the water drip( ?? )
Z||000003||VISCERAL||08-13-99||12:56 AM||||I have a mustang scoop here that I have to modify. Fits and looks like it should have been a factory option. But I dont know what to do about the screen mesh. I have to go to a hardware store like home depot or ace to see if they have anything that can work. I am beginning not to worry too much about the water. I'll put something near the opening on the decklid uder the scoop by the cut up edge that has an angle or graded lip to prevent water to flow directly down the middle, but let it flow down the sides toward the rear of the scoop.
Z||000004||mwbackus||08-13-99||04:25 AM||||Just a thought.. One of the most inovative engineering feats on the fiero was the design of the deck lid which incorporates an electro magnetic shield.  In later years this shielding was replaced with a special paint I believe.  If one was to cut out a good portion of the deck lid ie..shielding, one may conclude that some very undesirable effects may result (the ECM is quite sensitive to EM interference).  I have no idea of the severity of this issue, but, if GM justified the R&D costs for this, then I would say it could be quite a problem.<p>Mike
Z||000005||VISCERAL||08-13-99||08:13 AM||||I was wondering about that. I guess i'll just cut it somehow in a fashion that will leave the shielding intact. <p>HASN'T ANYONE HERE DONE THIS MOD TO THEIR CAR?   
Z||000006||Dale||08-13-99||12:17 PM||||Has anyone actualy figured out wich way the air flows through the deck lid
Z||000007||batboy||08-13-99||02:03 PM||||I don't know how to install those scoops, but the back window area of a Fiero, especially on the notchbacks, creates quite a low pressure area when the car is at speed. That's why the louvered vents are back there. The low pressure sucks hot air up out of those vents.<p>I'm not sure if those Mustang hood scoops are for drawing air in or out since the opening sits back farther to the rear. I'm guessing there is a lot of turbulent air in the slipstream at that point and the scoops are probably more for show than actual function.<p>Although, any attempt to increase ventilation into that tight engine compartment has to be good. Side air intake scoop(s) in conjunction with the hood scoop might be good. I'm fooling around with the idea of installing another side scoop on the passenger side since my battery has been relocated.
Z||000008||Cooter||08-13-99||04:51 PM||||Batboy- did you buy a battery relocation kit or just improvise one?
Z||000009||batboy||08-13-99||05:42 PM||||Cooter, I've ordered one of those metal battery relocating boxes from Chris West of West Coast Fiero's, but I haven't received it yet. You know, the heavy duty box that fits under the spare tire. Right now the battery is sitting in the rear luggage compartment which puts more unnecessary weight even further back on the rear end. You absolutely have to remove the battery from the factory location on a V8 conversion.
Z||000010||DXR_DAD||08-13-99||06:58 PM||||mwbackus,  <p>Left a e-mail with Tom (tmc87@hotmail.com)he sales the rear scoop. Ask about the sheild and how it is cut out.<p>Have not got a reply yet. But that is good info. <p>thanks
Z||000011||Bruce||08-13-99||07:22 PM||||Kind of on the same subject: has anyone received an update about the Holley-like side scoops that one of the FOCOA guys was going to make?
Z||000012||DXR_DAD||08-13-99||11:37 PM||||I got you scoop prepped. To mount you set in place with equal distance<br>agound the sides and back. make the holes then drill. the two that go<br>through the structure you need to back drill from the bottom just big enough<br>for the socket to fit through. The one that goes through the EMI plate has<br>two options. You can drill it and put a nut like the rest or remove the stud<br>and leave that one out. I have done them both ways. You can do this while<br>the lid is on the car as long as your careful. If you have any questions<br>please let me know.<p>Thjis is the info I got from Tom today. From what I can understand you must leave the EMI plate in place to mount the scoop. mwbackus, you were right. I will ask if and how much of the plate you can remove.
Z||000013||lowCG||08-14-99||02:13 AM||||I always liked the Fiat X-19 side scoops,probably where the GM boys ripped it off from anyways.You can put two per side,and they're self contained,just add a hole in your car.<br>The only reason that would make me want to put another hole in the deck lid,would be to add clearance for a rad motor.
Z||000014||DXR_DAD||08-14-99||11:18 PM||||More info from Tom, (tmc87@hotmail.com)<p>On mine the plate is in place. I didn t cut the hole real big. Also just to<br>let you know I have one fiero with out the plate and have never noticed any<br>ill effect. Also when pontiac stopped using the plate its because they mixed<br>metal in with the deck lid glass structure itself.<p>I hope this info is helpful. I am ready to put mine on as soon as I get it.
Z||000015||RICK||08-16-99||07:38 AM||||I just got a Mustang scoop this weekend from my frind that has a salvage yard, we started to put in on but my deck lid has the bump in it.  What year Fiero's did not have the bump above the engine?<br>Any of you guys that put the scoop on have the bump?  
Z||000016||TOM||08-18-99||11:16 PM||||RICK. The GT's have a flat decklid. All the rest have the hump. Except the 84 is flat but has the grate in the decklid where as the later ones have the vents.
